          "en": "Microsoft Develops AI for Space Weather Damage Prediction",
          "zh": "微软开发人工智能系统预测空间天气损害"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Microsoft Research developed a new machine learning system capable of predicting where space weather damage is likely to occur 30-60 minutes before a storm arrives.",
          "zh": "微软研究院开发了一种新的机器学习系统，能够在空间天气风暴来临前30-60分钟预测可能发生损害的区域。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "The machine learning system aims to predict damage from extreme space-weather events.",
            "These events can damage power systems, degrade GPS accuracy, and affect satellite operations.",
            "Predictions are available 30-60 minutes before a storm arrives."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "该机器学习系统旨在预测极端空间天气事件造成的损害。",
            "这些事件可能损害地球上的电力系统，降低GPS精度，并影响卫星运行。",
            "系统能够在风暴来临前30-60分钟提供预测。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This development demonstrates the application of machine learning in forecasting natural phenomena, providing a predictive capability for protecting critical infrastructure. It highlights AI's role in mitigating risks from space weather events on Earth.",
          "zh": "这一进展展示了机器学习在预测自然现象方面的应用，为保护关键基础设施提供了预测能力。它突出了人工智能在减轻地球上空间天气事件风险方面的作用。"
        },
        "source": "Microsoft Research",
        "link": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/forecasting-space-weather-risks-on-power-grids/"
      },
